# Bottom sheets & modals

Use Context **only** when the sheet or modal must open over `BottomBar` (tab screens + the floating tab bar). Every other screen keeps the overlay in that screen’s own state.

## When to use which

| Overlay lives on | State | Host the JSX |
| ---------------- | ----- | ------------ |
| A **tab** inside `BottomBar` (Home, Progress, Meals, Resources, More) | React Context — one `.tsx` file in `src/contexts/` | Render the sheet/modal in `src/navigation/BottomBar.tsx` so it sits above the tab bar |
| A **pushed screen** (MainStack / Auth / Onboarding — LogMeal, Settings, …) | `useState` on that screen | Render the sheet/modal in the screen (or a child it owns) |

```tsx
// ✅ tab (Meals) opens a sheet over BottomBar
const { openBottomSheet } = useSwapFoodBottomSheet();
openBottomSheet(suggestions);

// ✅ pushed screen — local state, no context
const [sheetIndex, setSheetIndex] = useState(-1);
<SelectFoodBottomSheet index={sheetIndex} onChange={setSheetIndex} />

// ❌ context for a Settings logout modal / LogMeal food picker
// ❌ mounting a BottomBar-hosted sheet inside the tab screen (clipped under the tab bar)
```

Do not create a context because “the sheet might be reused.” Reuse the component; only lift state to context when `BottomBar` must host it.

## BottomBar + Context (required steps)

1. **Context** — one file **directly** in `src/contexts/` (no subfolders): `src/contexts/<Name>BottomSheetContext.tsx` (or `*ModalContext.tsx`). Same pattern as `SwapFoodBottomSheetContext.tsx`, `FilterBottomSheetContext.tsx`, `MealHistoryFoodsBottomSheetContext.tsx`. Export `*Provider` and `use*` from that file.
2. **Provider** — wrap in `App.tsx` next to the existing sheet providers (`SwapFoodBottomSheetProvider`, `FilterBottomSheetProvider`, `MealHistoryFoodsBottomSheetProvider`).
3. **Host** — mount the sheet/modal once in `BottomBar.tsx` (sibling of the tab navigator / floating bar), wired to the context ref + index.
4. **Open from the tab** — the tab screen or its cards call `openBottomSheet(...)` / `closeBottomSheet()`. They do not render the sheet.

Context shape (match existing files):

- `openBottomSheet` / `closeBottomSheet`
- `bottomSheetRef` (`BottomSheetRef` from common `BottomSheet`)
- `bottomSheetIndex` (`-1` closed, `>= 0` open) + `onChange` / `handleSheetIndexChange`
- Optional payload state if the sheet needs ids or lists (`sheetPayload`, suggestions, filters)

The hook throws if used outside its provider.

Chrome is always common `BottomSheet` (see `ui-components.mdc`). Feature UI is `src/components/<feature>/<Name>BottomSheet.tsx`.

## Screen-local overlays

On any non-tab screen, keep a boolean or snap index in the screen:

```tsx
const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(false);
const [sheetIndex, setSheetIndex] = useState(-1);
```

Pass `visible` / `index` / `onClose` as props. Do not add a `src/contexts` file for these.

## Hard rules

- Context files live **directly** in `src/contexts/` (`src/contexts/FooBottomSheetContext.tsx`). Do not add `src/contexts/<feature>/` folders.
- Context sheets/modals are hosted in `BottomBar.tsx`, not in the tab’s screen tree.
- Tab code opens them through the context hook only.
- Pushed screens use internal state — no new context, no BottomBar mount.
- One context per BottomBar overlay; do not dump unrelated sheets into one provider.
